<title>USA: Airborne Express adds Anchorage flight.</title>
<headline>Airborne Express adds Anchorage flight.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airborne Express said it added a Saturday flight to its existing Anchorage, Alaska route from its Ohio hub from May 10.</p>
<p>The Anchorage station recorded a 38 percent growth rate over the last two years, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Airborne previously operated four flights from Tuesday to Friday on the route using a McDonnell Douglas DC-9. --Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
